        "Abstract": "Understanding expressions that refer to the physical world is crucial for human-assisting systems. We propose a multimodal reference resolution task and construct J-CRe3, a Japanese Conversation dataset for Real-world Reference Resolution. The dataset contains egocentric video and dialogue audio of real-world conversations between two people acting as a master and an assistant robot at home, annotated with crossmodal tags between phrases in the utterances and object bounding boxes in the video frames.",
